    "summary": "A photochemical cyclization reaction proceeding through a nitrene intermediate mechanism was conducted using 465 nm blue LEDs in acetonitrile solvent at 25°C and 0.1 M concentration. The continuous-flow photoreactor operated with a 10-minute residence time and 0.1 mL/min flow rate, achieving a 65% yield without requiring a photocatalyst. In comparison to the batch process, which required 10 hours (600 minutes) and only achieved 55% yield, the flow setup delivered a remarkable 60-fold reduction in reaction time while improving yield by 18.2%. The flow advantage stems from superior light intensity control and more efficient photon delivery in the continuous reactor design. This represents a significant process intensification with both time and yield benefits for the nitrene-mediated cyclization.",
