    "summary": "This process involves an intramolecular nucleophilic aromatic substitution (SNAr) cyclization reaction using DBU as base in diglyme solvent. The flow process operates at 220°C with a 30-minute residence time in a tubular plug flow reactor made of Hastelloy tubing (3.175 mm ID, 16.4 mL volume), using an HPLC pump at 8.3 mL/min flow rate and requiring a back-pressure regulator at 51.7 bar. Flow conditions achieved a 6-fold process intensification compared to batch, reducing reaction time from 3 hours to 30 minutes while increasing temperature from 140°C to 220°C. The flow setup enabled access to higher temperatures and pressures that would be challenging in batch mode, though the yield decreased slightly from 67% to 62%.",
